  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The energy of an electron in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math> Bohr orbit of a hydrogen atom can be calculated using the formula:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>Where</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>the</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>principal</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>quantum</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>the</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Bohr</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>orbit</mi><mo>.</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore, the energy of the electron in the third Bohr orbit of a hydrogen atom is&nbsp;Three times of this value.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
